            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p>Early Life of Alexander the Great<br>\nAlexander the Great was born in 356 BC in Pella, the ancient capital of Macedonia. He was tutored by the philosopher Aristotle, who instilled in him a passion for philosophy, medicine, and scientific investigation. Alexander's father, King Philip II, prepared him for leadership by involving him in governing Macedonia. When his father was assassinated in 336 BC, Alexander inherited a strong kingdom and an experienced army.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Campaigns Begin</strong><br>\nAlexander began his military campaigns against the Persian Empire in 334 BC. He won his first major battle at the River Granicus, followed by the liberation of the Asian Greek cities from Persian rule. His early victories demonstrated his military genius and the effectiveness of his well-trained Macedonian army, which included the formidable phalanx formation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Conquest of Syria and Egypt</strong><br>\nIn 332 BC, Alexander's forces defeated the Persian Army at Issus, which led to the surrender of Syria. He then moved south and captured Egypt, where he founded the city of Alexandria. The Egyptians welcomed Alexander as a liberator from Persian rule and crowned him as a pharaoh. In Egypt, he established a center of cultural and economic exchange that flourished for centuries.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
